.TH KOBAS 1 2000-1月 "kobas.term_similarity" "kobas.term_similarity"
.SH NAME
kobas.term_similarity \- Compute the pairwise similarity matrix of the given term list.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIkobas.term_similarity(\fBterms\fR as list, 
\fBmethod\fR as string = "kappa", 
\fBuniverse\fR as integer = -1, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Compute the pairwise similarity matrix of the given term list.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBterms\fB \fR\- 
 a named \fBlist\fR of the character vectors, the name of each slot is the term id
 and the value is the member gene id vector of that term (for example the result
 of \fBas.geneSet\fR of a gsea background model).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmethod\fB \fR\- the similarity method: \fBkappa\fR (Cohen's kappa, default) or \fBjaccard\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBuniverse\fB \fR\- 
 the size of the gene universe that is used by the kappa method. Default \fB-1\fR
 means the union size of all of the given terms.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a \fBdataframe\fR of the similarity matrix, both the row names and the column names
 are the term ids and the diagonal values are \fB1\fR.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
KOBAS
.SH FILES
.PP
gseakit.dll
.PP
